 !!! Note
     The minimum last stake amount can be configured using `last_stake_amount_min_ratio` - which defaults to 0.5 (50%). This means that the minimum stake amount that's ever used is `stake_amount * 0.5`. This avoids very low stake amounts, that are close to the minimum tradable amount for the pair and can be refused by the exchange.
 
+#### Currency exposure cap
+
+If you trade several pairs that are all priced against (or margined in) the same underlying currency - for example several USDT-margined futures, or several coins quoted in the same stablecoin - a losing move in that one currency can hit multiple open trades at once, even though each trade looked fine in isolation on its own.
+
+`max_currency_exposure` limits the combined stake committed, at any one time, to open trades whose pair shares the same quote currency, expressed as a ratio of the [tradable capital](#tradable-balance). It defaults to `1.0`, which does not restrict anything beyond the existing balance / `max_open_trades` limits.
+
+For example, with `tradable_balance_ratio=1` on a 1000 USDT account and `max_currency_exposure=0.5`, no more than 500 USDT may be committed at the same time to trades quoted in USDT - regardless of how many open trade slots `max_open_trades` would otherwise allow.
+
+When opening (or adding to, via [position adjustment](strategy-callbacks.md#adjust-trade-position)) a trade would push the combined exposure for that currency above the configured limit, the stake amount for that entry is reduced to fit under the limit - or the trade is skipped entirely if even the minimum tradable stake would no longer fit. This mirrors how [minimum/maximum stake limits](#minimum-trade-stake) are already enforced, and applies identically to live/dry-run trading and backtesting.
+
+!!! Note
+    Freqtrade currently requires all whitelisted pairs to share the bot's configured `stake_currency`. This means that, in normal use, this setting caps the combined stake tied up in *all* simultaneously open trades to the configured ratio of tradable capital.
+
 #### Static stake amount
 
 The `stake_amount` configuration statically configures the amount of stake-currency your bot will use for each trade.
